Keil (ARM Compiler 5) support patch for cmsis-device-f4.
Applied automatically by cmake/dependencies.cmake after the pinned checkout.

File: Source/Templates/arm/startup_stm32f407xx.s
Why:  the CubeMX default main/ISR stack is 1 KB. The GCC path reserves 4 KB via
      _Min_Stack_Size in projects/stm32f407/stm32f407ve.ld, and this ARM startup
      file is the one the Keil target assembles (the GCC target assembles
      Source/Templates/gcc/). Without this the Keil build would run on a quarter
      of the intended stack, silently.
Note: Heap_Size is left at the 512 B default. It is unused -- the firmware is
      built with configSUPPORT_DYNAMIC_ALLOCATION 0 and never calls malloc.

Apply from device-src: git apply ../patches/device-arm-startup-stack.patch

diff --git a/Source/Templates/arm/startup_stm32f407xx.s b/Source/Templates/arm/startup_stm32f407xx.s
index dcbfbb0..81c058f 100644
--- a/Source/Templates/arm/startup_stm32f407xx.s
+++ b/Source/Templates/arm/startup_stm32f407xx.s
@@ -29,7 +29,13 @@
 ;   <o> Stack Size (in Bytes) <0x0-0xFFFFFFFF:8>
 ; </h>
 
-Stack_Size      EQU     0x00000400
+; Raised from the CubeMX default of 0x400 to match _Min_Stack_Size in
+; projects/stm32f407/stm32f407ve.ld, so the ARM and GCC toolchains reserve the
+; same amount for the main/ISR stack. This file is only used by the Keil project
+; (the CMake/GNU build assembles Source/Templates/gcc/), and under Keil the
+; linker-provided stack is not used because __user_initial_stackheap below points
+; the C library at these areas -- so this value is what actually applies there.
+Stack_Size      EQU     0x00001000
 
                 AREA    STACK, NOINIT, READWRITE, ALIGN=3
 Stack_Mem       SPACE   Stack_Size
